   "source": "rag-fundamentals.md",
   "excerpt": "RAG systems introduce failure modes a database does not have: retrieval can\nmiss the relevant chunk, the model can ignore retrieved context, and the\nmodel can hallucinate details not present in any retrieved document.\nGrounding, citation, and evaluation of retrieval quality are therefore\nessential parts of a production RAG system.",
   "confidence": 0.9
  }
